    {
      "id": "word-es",
      "kind": "word",
      "promptEs": "es",
      "answerEn": "is; are (formal singular you)",
      "noteEn": "Es is a present form of ser for one person or thing, including usted, the formal way to address one person as 'you.' It can identify, classify, describe, evaluate, or state a time. Spanish can leave the person or thing understood, where English supplies 'he,' 'she,' or 'it.' Compare es with eres for familiar 'you' and son for several people or things.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Es una buena idea.",
        "en": "It is a good idea."
      },
